WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.588
The walkdown starts with equipment
identity,

2
00:00:02.708 --> 00:00:04.714
not a copied supplier checklist.

3
00:00:04.834 --> 00:00:07.671
Compare the vessel tag, manufacturer
model,

4
00:00:07.791 --> 00:00:11.247
serial number and location with the
controlled package.

5
00:00:11.367 --> 00:00:15.804
A matching tag attached to a different
vessel would not establish identity.

6
00:00:15.924 --> 00:00:20.063
Record discrepancies individually so a
later reviewer can tell

7
00:00:20.183 --> 00:00:23.511
which identifiers matched and which
remained uncertain.

8
00:00:24.131 --> 00:00:27.307
Work through the installed arrangement
systematically.

9
00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:31.779
Identify the agitator assembly and
supports, then trace the outlet

10
00:00:31.899 --> 00:00:35.194
and instrument connections against the
relevant drawing.

11
00:00:35.314 --> 00:00:38.364
Confirm required orientation and
accessible

12
00:00:38.484 --> 00:00:40.746
features using the approved method.

13
00:00:40.866 --> 00:00:44.684
Do not run the agitator to infer
installation conformity

14
00:00:44.804 --> 00:00:48.026
when the authorized activity is a static
inspection.

15
00:00:48.146 --> 00:00:52.007
Functional rotation checks belong in the
defined test plan.

16
00:00:52.627 --> 00:00:56.552
The design allowed a rear instrument to
slide out for maintenance,

17
00:00:56.672 --> 00:01:00.278
but the installed pipe rack crosses that
removal envelope.

18
00:01:00.398 --> 00:01:03.342
A front-facing photograph misses this
problem.

19
00:01:03.462 --> 00:01:06.697
Compare the full maintenance envelope with
the approved

20
00:01:06.817 --> 00:01:09.569
arrangement and manufacturer requirements.

21
00:01:09.689 --> 00:01:12.249
No universal clearance is supplied here.

22
00:01:12.369 --> 00:01:15.334
Document the obstruction and its
consequences

23
00:01:15.454 --> 00:01:18.526
without inventing a numerical GMP minimum.

24
00:01:19.146 --> 00:01:23.136
A covered connection cannot be recorded as
verified solely

25
00:01:23.256 --> 00:01:25.256
because its neighbour matches.

26
00:01:25.376 --> 00:01:28.085
Record the inaccessible item, why it could

27
00:01:28.205 --> 00:01:30.808
not be examined and the agreed follow-up.

28
00:01:30.928 --> 00:01:33.765
If suitable controlled evidence supports
another

29
00:01:33.885 --> 00:01:37.213
verification method, justify its
applicability.

30
00:01:37.333 --> 00:01:42.048
Distinguish direct observation from
document review so the evidence does

31
00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:44.168
not appear stronger than it is.
